2026-11-12T02:13:18.618-08:00 [writer] RECEIVED topic="s0036_tasks" correlation_id="a322b8ac-c8d6-430e-9aa2-1bb11e96db35" partition=0 offset=222 kind="task"
2026-11-12T02:13:25.980-08:00 [writer] SENT topic="s0036_drafts" correlation_id="a322b8ac-c8d6-430e-9aa2-1bb11e96db35" plan=["Check vulnerable Spring versions", "Prioritize by exposure and criticality", "Patch highest-priority service first"] draft="Based on the s0036_rel advisory (VULN-0036-HW9-06, id 20079), all services using `spring-beans` >=5.3.0 but <5.3.18 are vulnerable to **critical severity CVE-2022-22965** (Remote code execution via Spring4Shell on JDK 9+). Since every service shares the same vulnerable component and the vulnerability has identical critical impact across all instances, **prioritize patching all services to the fixed version (5.3.18) immediately**. There is no distinction in exposure risk between services here\u2014the critical RCE vulnerability affects all systems using the vulnerable Spring version range equally. Delaying patching risks unmitigated remote code execution. Therefore, the highest-priority action is to deploy the fix (5.3.18) universally without service-specific differentiation. (148 words)\n\nSource record: VULN-0036-HW9-06 (s0036_rel id 20079): spring-beans affected >= 5.3.0, < 5.3.18, severity critical. CVE-2022-22965: Remote code execution through data binding on JDK 9+ (Spring4Shell). Fixed in 5.3.18."
